            <details class="project-item" id="project2" name="projects">
                <summary class="project-header">
                    <img src="/project_images/alzheimers_cover.png" alt="" loading="lazy" class="project-image">
                    <span class="project-header-text">
                        <span class="project-title">Alzheimer's Detection</span>
                        <span class="project-date">August 2024 – December 2024</span>
                        <span class="project-description">Compared CNN, logistic regression, and SVM models for Alzheimer's stage classification on the OASIS MRI dataset.</span>
                    </span>
                    <span class="project-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </summary>
                <div class="project-expanded" id="project2-expanded">
                    <p><strong>Live Demo:</strong> <a href="https://earlyalzheimerdetection.streamlit.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">earlyalzheimerdetection.streamlit.app</a></p>
                    <p><strong>GitHub Repository:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/etan630/Alzheimer-Detection" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">github.com/etan630/Alzheimer-Detection</a></p>
                    <h3>Project Overview</h3>
                    <p>Built and compared models in TensorFlow and scikit-learn. Preprocessing included normalization, grayscale conversion, principal component analysis (PCA), and data augmentation. Used Grad-CAM to inspect which regions of MRI slices influenced the CNN's predictions.</p>

                    <h3>Dataset</h3>
                    <p>Used the OASIS MRI dataset, containing over 80,000 MRI scans labeled with varying levels of dementia: Non-Demented, Very Mild, Mild, and Moderate. The dataset was split into 70% training, 20% testing, and 10% validation subsets to train and evaluate the models.</p>

                    <h3>Machine Learning Models</h3>
                    <h4>Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)</h4>
                    <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> CNNs excel at image classification tasks by detecting complex spatial patterns in image data.</p>
                    <p><strong>Model Layers:</strong></p>
                    <ul class="styled-list">
                        <li>Rescaling Layer: Normalizes pixel values to a range of [0,1].</li>
                        <li>Convolutional Layers (Conv2D): Extracts spatial features through sliding kernels.</li>
                        <li>MaxPooling2D: Reduces spatial dimensions to focus on prominent features.</li>
                        <li>Dense Layers: Implements fully connected layers for classification.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Preprocessing:</strong></p>
                    <ul class="styled-list">
                        <li>Feature normalization by dividing pixel values by 255.</li>
                        <li>Random adjustments for brightness and zoom, and horizontal flips for data augmentation.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p><strong>Performance Metrics:</strong></p>
                    <p>Accuracy: 99.97% &nbsp;|&nbsp; Precision, Recall, and F1-Score: &gt;99.9% across all metrics.</p>
                    <p><img src="/project_images/gradcam.png" alt="Grad-CAM Visualization" />
                        Grad-CAM highlighted regions of the MRI scan that influenced the CNN's prediction.</p>

                    <h4>Logistic Regression</h4>
                    <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Acts as a baseline classification model with high computational efficiency.</p>
                    <p><strong>Preprocessing:</strong> Grayscale conversion, PCA for dimensionality reduction, L2 regularization to minimize overfitting.</p>
                    <p><strong>Performance:</strong> Accuracy: 92.43% (before balancing), 90.44% (after balancing). Balanced F1-Score: ~93%.</p>

                    <h4>Support Vector Machine (SVM)</h4>
                    <p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Designed for high-dimensional data with a focus on clear class boundaries.</p>
                    <p><strong>Preprocessing:</strong> Grayscale conversion, PCA, class weighting to address data imbalance.</p>
                    <p><strong>Performance:</strong> Accuracy: 76.46% &nbsp;|&nbsp; F1-Score: 78.58%</p>

                    <h3>Future Directions</h3>
                    <ul class="styled-list">
                        <li>Incorporating more diverse datasets to improve generalizability.</li>
                        <li>Retraining CNNs on balanced datasets to evaluate performance under controlled conditions.</li>
                        <li>Exploring additional models and ensemble methods to enhance accuracy and robustness.</li>
                        <li>Implement logic for user to import a photo to test for Alzheimer's stage.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <button class="ink-link project-close" type="button" hidden>Close project <span aria-hidden="true">↑</span></button>
